        {
          "page": 3,
          "section": "2. Materials and methods",
          "quote": "Under an argon atmosphere, equiatomic TiZrNbTa alloy ingots (about 25 g) were prepared by arc melting. First, the ZrTa master alloy with an atomic ratio of 1:1 was prepared. To ensure chemical uniformity, each alloy ingot was flipped and remelted five times. TiZrNbTa HEA was then prepared, each alloy ingot was flipped and remelted seven times, and each melt was kept in the liquid state for five minutes.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "85000a75e9a0a4b5:part:001"
